Environment Variables in GitHub Actions

Today I learned how environment variables make workflows flexible by storing reusable values like paths, flags, and configuration settings.

🔹 env Keyword
env is used to define environment variables in workflows.
 It helps avoid hardcoding values and makes pipelines easier to maintain.

🔹 Job-level vs Step-level Variables
Job-level env applies to all steps in that job
Step-level env applies only to one step
Step-level variables override job-level values
This gives precise control of configuration.

🔹 Default Environment Variables
GitHub provides built-in variables automatically, like:
Repository info
Workflow info
Runner details
Commit/branch context
These are useful for dynamic CI/CD behavior.

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Env vars improve reuse.
 Scope controls visibility.
 Defaults add context.
